---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../config";

const mail = `mailto:${site.contactEmail}`;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`What ${site.name} collects, why, who else processes it, and how to get it deleted.`}
  updated={site.legalUpdated}
>
  <p>
    This policy covers the hosted {site.name} service at <strong>app.rakumi.app</strong>, this website, and the
    waitlist. {site.operator} runs {site.name} as an independent developer in Maryland, USA ("we", "us").
  </p>
  <p>
    If you self-host {site.name}, your data stays on your own server. We cannot see it, and this policy does
    not apply to it.
  </p>

  <h2>Short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We collect only what we need to run and improve the app.</li>
    <li>We do not sell your data. We do not show ads. Our analytics show how people use {site.name}, not who they are.</li>
    <li>We never see your card number. Our payment partner handles it.</li>
    <li>When your plan ends, we delete your household's data after 30 days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Email address and password</td><td>To sign you in, verify your email, and reset your password.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Household name and what you add: recipes, pantry items, meal plans, shopping lists, cooking history, and dietary rules</td><td>This is the app. We store it so you and your household can use it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Plan and payment status (trial, active, cancelled, dates)</td><td>To know if your household has access.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>API tokens you create</td><td>To let tools such as an AI assistant connect to your household.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>IP address</td><td>To deliver pages and to block abuse, such as too many log-in attempts.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Usage data: pages you visit, features you use, browser and device type, and approximate country</td><td>To learn which parts of {site.name} help people and what to improve. We do not use it for ads, and we do not sell it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Waitlist email address</td><td>To tell you when {site.name} opens and to send you occasional product updates.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Emails you send us</td><td>To answer you.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    The app uses one cookie to keep you signed in. It lasts up to 30 days, or until you log out. The app also
    saves some settings on your device, such as your color theme.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app and this website use analytics to collect usage data. We do not use advertising or cross-site tracking
    cookies. If our analytics tool sets a cookie, we name the cookie here.
  </p>

  <h2>Who else processes your data</h2>
  <p>We use these services to run {site.name}. Each one gets only the data it needs.</p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Service</th><th scope="col">What it does</th><th scope="col">Data it gets</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://polar.sh/legal/privacy">Polar</a></td>
        <td>Sells the subscription as merchant of record: checkout, payment, tax, receipts, and billing portal.</td>
        <td>Email, name, payment details, billing address.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy">Resend</a></td>
        <td>Sends emails: verification, password reset, account warnings, and waitlist emails. Stores the waitlist.</td>
        <td>Email address and the email content.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare</a></td>
        <td>Hosts this website, connects the app to the internet, and protects it from attacks.</td>
        <td>IP address and the traffic between your browser and {site.name}.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Analytics service</td>
        <td>Counts page views and feature use, so we can see how people use {site.name}.</td>
        <td>Usage data (see above). The analytics service does not get your recipes, pantry, or plans.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The app server and its database run on hardware we own, in Maryland, USA. Your data is stored in the
    United States.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you connect an AI assistant or another tool to {site.name}, that tool can read and change your household
    data. Its own privacy policy applies to what it does with the data.
  </p>
  <p>We share data with others only if the law requires it.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Household data:</strong> while your plan is active. When your plan ends or a payment fails, your
      household locks. 30 days after the lock, we delete the household, its accounts, and all its data. We send
      warning emails before we delete it.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Payment records:</strong> Polar keeps them as tax law requires. When we delete your household, we also ask Polar to delete your customer record.</li>
    <li><strong>Waitlist:</strong> until you unsubscribe (use the link in any waitlist email) or ask us to remove you.</li>
    <li><strong>Support emails:</strong> as long as we need them to help you.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>Email <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a> from the address on your account to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Get a copy of your data.</li>
    <li>Correct your data.</li>
    <li>Delete your account and data now, without waiting 30 days.</li>
    <li>Ask what data we have about you.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We answer within 30 days. We give these rights to everyone, wherever you live.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    Connections use HTTPS. We protect passwords and sign-in data with standard security practices. No system is
    perfectly secure. If we learn of a breach that affects your data, we will email you.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is not for children under 13. We do not knowingly collect data from them. If you think a child under
    13 gave us data, email us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will update the date at the top when this policy changes. If a change is important, we will email account
    holders before it takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {site.operator}, Maryland, USA. Email <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
